      "rationale": "Both tests exercise sqlparse.format(..., reindent_aligned=True), which uses AlignedIndentFilter._split_kwds to right-align split keywords (FROM/JOIN/GROUP BY, etc.) within a fixed-width column sized to len('select'). The filter's own comment (\"only consider the first word as aligner\") and the pre-existing GROUP/ORDER BY compensation hack (offset_ = 3) show the intended design uses only the first word of a multi-word keyword (e.g. \"LEFT\" of \"LEFT JOIN\", \"GROUP\" of \"GROUP BY\") to compute padding; the regression instead uses the whole phrase, producing a negative/zero pad for anything longer than \"select\" and misaligning those lines by exactly the amount shown. The expected strings were derived by hand-tracing the documented algorithm (max keyword width 6, offset_ = 3 hack for GROUP/ORDER BY) rather than from the buggy code's current output.",
